# {{name}}

{{#if description}}{{description}}

{{/if}}A {{framework}} agent generated by [Armature](https://github.com/gnsepili/armature) from
`armature.yaml`. It is a plain Python project: it does not depend on Armature at runtime.

## Run it

```bash
uv venv && uv pip install -e ".[dev]"
cp .env.example .env   # then set {{model.api_key_env}}
python -m {{package}} chat     # talk to the agent in the terminal
python -m {{package}} serve    # ARC HTTP server on http://127.0.0.1:8000
```

Set `ARMATURE_MODEL_MODE=mock` to run against the offline mock LLM instead of {{model.provider}}.

## What you own

| Path | Owner |
| --- | --- |
| `src/{{package}}/tools/*.py` | You. Implement each tool's `run` function. |
| `src/{{package}}/prompts/system.md` | You. The system prompt. |
| `tests/test_tools.py`, this README | You. |
| everything else | Armature. Change `armature.yaml` and run `armature generate`. |

Armature never overwrites a file you edited: a managed file you change stops being updated
and `armature generate` tells you so.

